      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How to use\n\n**What it does:** loads a video, MMAudio listens to the frames and writes a matching sound track (the Synchformer lines the sounds up with the motion), then saves the same video with the new audio. MMAudio 44 kHz.\n\n**Inputs**\n1. **Load Video**: your clip (for example a Wan or LTX render). Its frames and fps are reused, the picture is not changed.\n2. **Prompt**: open the **Audio (optional)** node (double-click) and type it on the **MMAudio Sampler**. Describe the sounds you want (wind, engine hum, footsteps), not the picture.\n\n**Settings (MMAudio Sampler)**\n| Setting | Default | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| duration | 8 | seconds of audio. Set it to your clip's length. |\n| steps | 25 | sampling steps |\n| cfg | 4.5 | how strongly the prompt is followed |\n| seed | randomize | set to fixed to repeat a result |\n| negative_prompt | empty | sounds to keep out |\n| mask_away_clip | off | on = the CLIP image features of the video are not used |\n| force_offload | on | moves the model off the GPU after the run |\n\nLoaders: model `mmaudio_large_44k_v2_fp16`, base precision fp16; feature utils in 44k mode, fp16.\n\n**Output:** Save Video writes the video with the new audio track to `ComfyUI/output/video/` (prefix `video/ComfyUI`).\n\n**Tips**\n- The images input of the sampler is optional: without a video MMAudio makes audio from the prompt alone (save it with a Save Audio node instead of Create Video).\n- MMAudio is light on VRAM.\n- Attention: --use-sage-attention used less VRAM at the same speed on the 24 GB bench server (measured on Z-Image, not on MMAudio). --use-ck-attention gave a different output for the same seed there.\n\n**Tested on:** no tested-on record yet. Checked on ComfyUI 0.45.3: the graph converts, but the ComfyUI-MMAudio pack did not import on that server (missing pip package `accelerate`), so it was not run there."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 506,
